<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Polemon I of Pontus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 8 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Polemon I was a Roman client king of Pontus and later of the Bosporan Kingdom in the late 1st century BCE. The son of the orator <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zeno-of-laodicea">Zeno of Laodicea</a>, he was made king of part of Pontus by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mark-antony">Mark Antony</a> in 37 BCE, kept his throne under Augustus and married Queen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pythodoris">Pythodorida</a>. He was killed around 8 BCE while campaigning against the Aspurgians near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sea-of-azov">Sea of Azov</a>.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Pharnaces II, Asander and his wife Dynamis, <b>Polemon</b> I and then Aspurgus ruled with Roman approval, and during the first century CE the kings took the names Tiberius Julius, styled themselves friends of Caesar and of the Romans, and placed the emperor’s portrait on their coins.</blockquote><a href="/empire/bosporan-kingdom">Bosporan Kingdom · Governance &amp; Law</a></li><li><blockquote>In 37 BCE Mark Antony made <b>Polemon</b>, son of the orator Zeno of Laodicea, king of part of the former Kingdom of Pontus.</blockquote><a href="/state/polemonid-pontus">Polemonid Pontus</a></li></ul></section>
